.\" newfs_ufsbe.8
.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
.Dd September 11, 2026
.Dt NEWFS_UFSBE 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm newfs_ufsbe
.Nd create a UFS2 filesystem for use with ufsbe
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl NUj
.Op Fl b Ar bsize
.Op Fl f Ar fsize
.Op Fl s Ar sectors
.Op Fl L Ar label
.Ar special
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
creates a UFS2 filesystem on
.Ar special
and sets the
.Dv FS_BETREE
flag
.Pq 0x00000800
in the superblock.
.Pp
It does this by first invoking
.Xr newfs 8
with
.Fl O Ar 2
and any additional options supplied, then reopening the resulting
superblock with
.Xr libufs 3
and OR-ing in
.Dv FS_BETREE .
.Pp
A filesystem created by
.Nm
must be mounted with
.Xr ufsbe 8
and checked with
.Xr fsck_ufsbe 8 .
Do not run
.Xr fsck_ffs 8
on such a filesystem; it will misinterpret the B-epsilon tree
block map as corruption.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl N
Dry-run: print the
.Xr newfs 8
command that would be run and the flag that would be set, but do
not write anything.
.It Fl U
Enable soft updates
.Pq default: on .
.It Fl j
Enable soft-update journaling
.Pq SUJ .
.It Fl b Ar bsize
Block size in bytes
.Pq default: 32768 .
.It Fl f Ar fsize
Fragment size in bytes
.Pq default: 4096 .
.It Fl s Ar sectors
Filesystem size in 512-byte sectors.
0 or omitted means use the whole device.
.It Fl L Ar label
Volume label.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Create a 4 GiB UFS2+softdep+FS_BETREE filesystem on a memory disk:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# truncate -s 4g disk.img
# mdconfig -a -t vnode -f disk.img
md0
# newfs_ufsbe -U /dev/md0
# ufsbe /dev/md0 /mnt
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ufsbe 8 ,
.Xr fsck_ufsbe 8 ,
.Xr newfs 8 ,
.Xr libufs 3
